  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05Q8">Definition <span data-tag="05Q8">4.27.20</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a category and let $S$ be a multiplicative system. We say $S$ is <em>saturated</em> if, in addition to MS1, MS2, MS3, we also have </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="MS4"><p>
Given three composable morphisms $f, g, h$, if $fg, gh \in S$, then $g \in S$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
